# race: new game -> licence -> difficulty -> sign up -> race start.
# Key path adapted from an earlier working sequence, reflowed onto the single-enter
# intro-skip prefix used by the other scenarios (see menu.keys).
#
# The race only runs without crashing from commit 1dfd778 onwards
# ("replay player input into the key buffer"). On anything
# earlier it crashes right after sign-up (Unhandled illegal instruction,
# _startRace). Run this scenario only on trees that include 1dfd778.
#
# enter, then shot:menu: reach the main menu (see menu.keys for why there
#   is no trailing Esc here anymore, and why one Enter -- not two -- is the
#   measured-reliable count).
# enter/enter: open "Start Racing" (default-highlighted), confirm
#   "Start A New Game" (also default-highlighted) -> Driver's Licence.
# t/e/s/t + enter: type nickname "TEST", confirm.
# enter: weapons YES (default) -> "Select difficulty" popup.
# enter: default difficulty -> "Welcome to Death Rally" popup over sign-up.
# enter: dismiss it -> "PRESS ENTER TO SIGN UP" (easy race preselected).
# enter, then a long wait: signs up; the race screen takes about 20s to
#   load and lands on the first-race popup ("PRESS ENTER TO CONTINUE").
# enter: dismisses the popup: countdown, race runs.
#
# Verified with screenshots on a build including 1dfd778: reaches the
# Driver's Licence, the difficulty popup, the sign-up screen, and a running
# race with AI cars moving, 0 Unhandled (also re-verified
# with the Esc-free prefix and the RUN_SECS-derived keys bound).
enter w3500
shot:menu
enter w1500
enter w1500
t w200
e w200
s w200
t w200
enter w1200
enter w1500
enter w3000
enter w2500
enter w20000
enter w2000
